NAME
       find - search for files in a directory hierarchy

SYNOPSIS
       find [PATH]... [EXPRESSION]

DESCRIPTION
       Walk the directory tree rooted at each PATH (default .) and evaluate
       EXPRESSION for every file. Tests are joined with AND unless separated by
       -o. When the expression has no action, matching paths are printed.

OPTIONS
       -name PATTERN
           base name matches shell PATTERN (*, ?, [...])

       -iname PATTERN
           like -name, case insensitive

       -path PATTERN
           whole path matches PATTERN

       -type f|d|l
           file is a regular file, directory or link

       -size [+-]N[ckMG]
           size is more (+), less (-) or exactly N units (512-byte blocks by
           default)

       -mtime [+-]N
           modified N days ago

       -newer FILE
           modified more recently than FILE

       -perm MODE
           permission bits are exactly MODE (octal)

       -empty
           empty file or directory

       -maxdepth N, -mindepth N
           limit the depth of the search

       ! EXPR, -not EXPR
           negate the next test

       -o
           logical OR between tests

       -print, -print0
           print the path, followed by a newline or a NUL

       -exec CMD {} ;
           run CMD with {} replaced by the path; true if CMD exits 0

       -delete
           delete matching files (depth first)

EXAMPLES
       find / -name '*.c'
       find /root -type d -empty
       find . -name '*.o' -delete
       find . -size +1M -exec ls -lh {} ;

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), grep(1), xargs(1), tree(1)
